```yaml
spec:
  grid: 5-7 rows x 4-7 cols
  background: single color, most common (~60-67% of cells)
  neutral_mask:
    color: single foreground color, must be uniquely most frequent foreground color
    components: 2-3 4-connected polyominoes, size 2-5 each
    separation: min manhattan distance >=2 between any two components
  markers:
    count: 2-4 distinct colors, each exactly 1 pixel
    touching: each marker is either 4-adjacent to exactly one neutral component or isolated (distractor)
    constraint: each neutral component touches at most 1 marker color
    distractors: 0-1 markers that touch no neutral component [observed]
  untouched_components: 0-1 neutral components with no adjacent marker [observed]
  output:
    same grid size; markers erased to bg; each touched neutral component recolored to its marker color; untouched components stay neutral

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (5-7 x 4-7), bg color, neutral color, and 2-4 marker colors (all distinct).
    2. Place 2-3 polyominoes (size 2-5) on the grid with min manhattan gap >=2 between them. These are the neutral components in the output (but colored by marker colors).
    3. Assign each component a unique marker color (one component may remain unassigned = stays neutral).
    4. Build the output grid: bg everywhere, colored components placed, unassigned components in neutral.
    5. Derive input from output: recolor all assigned components back to neutral color. For each assigned component, place its marker color as a single pixel 4-adjacent to the component (on a bg cell). Optionally place 0-1 distractor marker pixels isolated from all components.
    6. Validate: neutral pixel count > any single marker pixel count (=1), ensuring neutral is uniquely most frequent foreground color.
